<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (Pentecostalism is a vibrant and dynamic branch of Christianity characterized by an emphasis on the personal experience of the Holy Spirit. Believers seek to encounter the Spirit's power through experiences such as Spirit baptism, evidenced by speaking in tongues, and the operation of spiritual gifts. Pentecostals prioritize passionate worship, fervent prayer, and a commitment to spreading the gospel with signs and wonders. Their faith is marked by a deep reliance on the Holy Spirit for spiritual empowerment, leading to a vibrant expression of Christianity focused on personal transformation, community, and evangelism.)
/E (Pentecostalism is a vibrant and dynamic branch of Christianity characterized by an emphasis on the personal experience of the Holy Spirit. Believers seek to encounter the Spirit's power through experiences such as Spirit baptism, evidenced by speaking in tongues, and the operation of spiritual gifts. Pentecostals prioritize passionate worship, fervent prayer, and a commitment to spreading the gospel with signs and wonders. Their faith is marked by a deep reliance on the Holy Spirit for spiritual empowerment, leading to a vibrant expression of Christianity focused on personal transformation, community, and evangelism.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [3]
>>
